Requirement:
"""
Make the shortener safer — people are abusing it. Also block URL shorteners chaining to other shorteners.
"""

Answers to earlier questions:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "ambiguityId": "AMB-1",
      "answer": "Malicious destination URLs. Flooding is covered by the rate limiter; spam accounts are out of scope."
    },
    {
      "ambiguityId": "AMB-2",
      "answer": "Block at creation for domains on our blocklist. For existing links, an admin can flag a link; a flagged link answers 451 instead of redirecting."
    },
    {
      "ambiguityId": "AMB-3",
      "answer": "No external API: a domain blocklist in configuration, matched with all subdomains."
    },
    {
      "ambiguityId": "AMB-4",
      "answer": "No rescan. Admin flagging handles links that already exist."
    }
  ]
}

